      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "As longevity increases in HIV-infected individuals after the introduction of highly active antiretroviral therapy regimens, long-term effects such as cardiovascular disease and, more specifically, symptomatic heart failure are emerging as leading health issues. In the present review article, we discuss HIV-associated cardiovascular disease, focusing on etiopathogenetic mechanisms that may play a role in diagnosis, management, and therapy of HIV-associated heart failure in the highly active antiretroviral therapy era."},
